  "scope": "Paired decider queries on live frames of the 99 wars declared on us in the\n2026-11-18/19 live Deity games (6 players, Small Continents, Online) that\nbrought an enemy soldier within two tiles of the original capital (33 that took\nit, 66 that did not; four more runs were pruned from the host), each on the\ndeclaration turn: the first state row on which the war shows.\n\n`mobilization-hears-the-declaration` is the only bit that varies. Each case is\na live run's own events.jsonl cut after the FIRST state row of turn N (it holds\nthe mod's `diplomacy_choice` declaration line, which precedes that row),\nreplayed at turn N. Both arms run one frozen `civvis_orders --resumed` built\nfrom the branch (profile ci), with that run's own requested genome (why.log\nline 1 `forced`, each as `--with`; it carries `surprise-war-mobilization`);\nthe on arm adds `--with mobilization-hears-the-declaration`.\n\nRead per arm, from the proposed orders: the count of each order kind\n(`produce`, `purchase`, upgrades, policy changes, ...) and whether the orders\ndiffer between the arms.\n\nThis records proposal activation on captured live input only. It does not\nexecute in Civ VI, replays one turn at a time from the live board, and makes no\nclaim that a city holds.",
